description: Code style rules for JS/TS/Vue files
globs: "**/*.{js,ts,vue}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Code Style

- No semicolons
- Single quotes for strings
- 2-space indentation
- No trailing commas
- Arrow parens: avoid when possible (`x => x` not `(x) => x`)
- Line width: 100 characters max
- LF line endings (not CRLF)

## TypeScript

- Use TypeScript for new files in `src/renderer/stores/` and `src/common/`
- Prefer explicit types for function parameters and return values
- `any` is allowed during gradual migration but avoid in new code
- Use path aliases: `@/` for `src/renderer/`, `common/` for `src/common/`

## Vue

- Use `<script setup>` for new Vue components
- Use Composition API (not Options API)
- Component names: PascalCase in templates, kebab-case filenames
